## 🔍 Key Architecture Decisions

### VFS Query Pattern
```groq
*[_type == "product" && count(catalogueLocationKeys[@ in $catalogueKeys]) > 0]
```
**Rationale:** O(1) array intersection instead of O(n) string matching. Uses Sanity's GROQ `@ in` operator for efficient filtering.

### Key Unrolling Algorithm
```typescript
// Stack-based DFS to collect all descendant IDs
const unrollDescendantKeys = (nodeId: string): string[] => {
  const result = new Set<string>();
  const stack = [nodeId];
  
  while (stack.length > 0) {
    const currentId = stack.pop()!;
    if (result.has(currentId)) continue;
    
    result.add(currentId);
    const children = slotMetadataMap[currentId]?.children || [];
    stack.push(...children);
  }
  
  return Array.from(result);
};
```
**Rationale:** Handles arbitrary tree depth, prevents cycles with Set, O(n) complexity.

### Empty Keys = All Products
When `catalogueKeys` is empty array, `getSelectedProducts()` returns all products.
**Rationale:** Supports "All Products" page without special-casing the query.

